OWNER_FAIL_FAST_STRUCTURAL_20261006.txt.text:
OWNER DIRECTIVE (2026-10-06 ~21:00): if the CURRENT route of a redesigned block misses (SS < +15 or FF < +15 after the automatic hold ECO), the NEXT step is an AGGRESSIVE structural fix that accepts a performance penalty. No more minimal attempts. Pick whatever closes fastest:
- more pipeline stages on every path in the failing classes, plus everything within 100 ps of them (+1..+3 cycles OK);
- split the block further (<= ~0.5 mm leaves) with registered hops;
- narrow or halve a datapath and run it 2x longer (II 2), or put a non-critical unit on a slower / half-rate clock with a registered CDC;
- convert long combinational reductions and shift-register delay lines into pipelined trees / SRAM FIFOs.
Price the cost (cycles, then % of AR/MTP) in the block record and report it. A few % of headline per block is acceptable; flag anything above ~3% to the main session BEFORE adopting it. Keep exactness transaction-level and the negative controls failing.

OWNER_SAFE_VARIANT_20261006.txt.text:
OWNER DIRECTIVE (2026-10-06 ~21:10): for the HIGH-RISK blocks, build a "SAFE" version NOW and route it IN PARALLEL with the current route; don't wait for the current one to fail.
Blocks: DS PQ q-element, DS fused head, DS softmax, HBM SM, HBM W2, HBM attention-tile assembly, HBM SU controller + reducer. (Optional, if cheap: HBM router, DS code-pair, DS WFC src.)
The SAFE version is designed to close easily, accepting a performance penalty:
- every path in the last route's failing classes, and every path within 150 ps of failing, gets +1..+3 register stages;
- leaves of <= ~0.5 mm with registered latency-insensitive boundaries; no block-internal clock tree deeper than the budget target;
- halve hot datapaths (II 2 / 2x cycles) wherever one stage is still deep; SRAM/FIFO for long delay lines; pipelined reduction trees;
- route target 730 ps (sign-off 833.333), HM 35, closure loop with calibrate + auto hold ECO.
Exactness stays transaction-level, with the negative controls failing. Price the SAFE version's cycle/throughput cost.
ADOPTION: whichever version closes first (SS >= +15 / FF >= +15) is adopted. If both close, adopt the faster one. Flag the SAFE cost to the main session if it is above ~3% of the target's AR/MTP headline.
This is an explicit owner exception to the one-route rule: max 2 routes per block (current + SAFE).

